# {{ app_name }} - Python agent service

## Stack
- Python {{ versions.python }}, FastAPI {{ versions.fastapi }}, uv ({{ versions.uv }}) with a committed `uv.lock`
- pytest, ruff, mypy (strict). The tests and the evaluation run use the fake provider: no network, no key
- One provider interface with two implementations: a deterministic fake and the Claude API adapter (`AGENT_CLAUDE_MODEL`, key from `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`)
- Hosting is the project owner's choice (see the `deployment` skill, `.agents/skills/deployment/SKILL.md`)

## Structure
```
{{ app_path }}/app/main.py            -> create_app(): fail-closed startup, wiring
{{ app_path }}/app/auth/              -> bearer JWT verification against a JWKS (no shared secret)
{{ app_path }}/app/agent/turn.py      -> one agent turn: provider, tools, data envelopes
{{ app_path }}/app/providers/         -> provider interface, fake, Claude adapter
{{ app_path }}/app/tools/             -> read-only tools; get_my_profile calls GET /api/me with the user's token
{{ app_path }}/app/safety/            -> untrusted-data envelopes, budget, audit log, notice
{{ app_path }}/openapi.yml            -> this service's own contract
{{ app_path }}/evals/                 -> evaluation cases and the runner
```

## Rules
- The service assists and does not advise. Every response carries the notice (`app/safety/notice.py`)
- The question and every tool result are untrusted data: they travel in `<untrusted-data>` envelopes and never reach the system prompt
- Tools only read, and use the caller's own token for every backend call; the model never picks a URL or a user
- Every tool call is logged with the user and request IDs, never with a token or a value
- A per-user budget is enforced in memory; there is no cross-user state
- Startup fails with no identity configured, or with the `local` profile next to a real issuer. The service has no dev-identity endpoint and no switch that turns authentication off
- No API key in any file

## Commands
- `task {{ app_id }}:dev` (profile `local`, port {{ port }}; the backend runs under its `local` profile)
- `task {{ app_id }}:test`, `task {{ app_id }}:lint`, `task {{ app_id }}:typecheck`, `task {{ app_id }}:eval`
